    {
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You eked out a living by picking pockets on the streets of a major city, never knowing where you'd find your next meal. While some folk adventure for the glory, you do so to survive.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "Choose two ability boosts. One must be to ",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "content": "Dexterity",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": true,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "content": " or ",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "content": "Constitution",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": true,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "content": ", and one is a free ability boost.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You're trained in the Thievery skill and a Lore skill for the city you lived in as a street urchin (such as Absalom Lore or Magnimar Lore). You gain the ",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "display": "Pickpocket",
              "kind": "crossref",
              "targetId": "feat/pickpocket"
            },
            {
              "content": " skill feat.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "name": "Street Urchin",
      "slug": "street-urchin",
      "traits": [],
      "type": "background"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "passive",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You can Steal or Palm an Object that's closely guarded, such as in a pocket, without taking the -5 penalty. You can't steal objects that would be extremely noticeable or time consuming to remove (like worn shoes or armor or actively wielded objects). If you're a master in Thievery, you can attempt to Steal from a creature in combat or otherwise on guard. When doing so, Stealing requires 2 manipulate actions instead of 1, and you take a -5 penalty.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "name": "Pickpocket",
      "slug": "pickpocket",
      "traits": [
        "general",
        "skill"
      ],
      "type": "feat"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "passive",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You were raised to be ambitious and always reach for the stars, leading you to progress quickly in your chosen field. You gain a 1st-level class feat for your class. You must meet the prerequisites, but you can select the feat later in the character creation process in order to determine which prerequisites you meet.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "name": "Natural Ambition",
      "slug": "natural-ambition",
      "traits": [
        "human"
      ],
      "type": "feat"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "2",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "With a quick sprint, you dash up to your foe and swing. Stride twice. If you end your movement within melee reach of at least one enemy, you can make a melee Strike against that enemy. You can use Sudden Charge while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "name": "Sudden Charge",
      "slug": "sudden-charge",
      "traits": [
        "barbarian",
        "fighter",
        "flourish"
      ],
      "type": "feat"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "passive",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "The short human life span lends perspective and has taught you from a young age to set aside differences and work with others to achieve greatness. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus on checks to Aid.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "name": "Cooperative Nature",
      "slug": "cooperative-nature",
      "traits": [
        "human"
      ],
      "type": "feat"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "reaction",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "Trigger",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": true,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "content": " An enemy hits you with a melee strike.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "kind": "divider"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You can snap your shield into place just as you would take a blow, avoiding the hit at the last second. You immediately use the ",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "display": "Raise a Shield",
              "kind": "crossref",
              "targetId": "action/raise-a-shield"
            },
            {
              "content": " action and gain your shield's bonus to AC. The circumstance bonus from the shield applies to your AC when you're determining the outcome of the triggering attack.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "name": "Reactive Shield",
      "slug": "reactive-shield",
      "traits": [
        "fighter"
      ],
      "type": "feat"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "passive",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "Choose a deity and cause as you would if you were a champion. You become trained in light, medium, and heavy armor. You become trained in Religion and your deity's associated skill; for each of these skills in which you were already trained, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You become trained in champion class DC.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You are bound by your deity's anathema and must follow the champion's code and alignment requirements for your cause. You don't gain any other abilities from your choice of deity or cause.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "kind": "divider"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "Special",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": true,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "content": " You cannot select another dedication feat until you have gained two other feats from the ",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            },
            {
              "display": "Champion",
              "kind": "crossref",
              "targetId": "archetype/champion"
            },
            {
              "content": " archetype.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "name": "Champion Dedication (Iomedae)",
      "slug": "champion-dedication-iomedae",
      "traits": [
        "archetype",
        "dedication",
        "multiclass"
      ],
      "type": "feat"
    },
    {
      "actionCost": "passive",
      "body": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "content": "You gain the appropriate devotion spell for your cause (lay on hands for the paladin, redeemer, and liberator). If you don't already have one, you gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point, which you can Refocus by praying or serving your deity.",
              "kind": "text",
              "marks": {
                "bold": false,
                "italic": false,
                "superscript": false
              }
            }
          ],
          "kind": "paragraph"
